Problem: BGMI/PUBG Match System

Phase 1: Basic Match Creation & Player Management
Problem Statement: Design a system to manage BGMI matches where players can join lobbies and start games.

Requirements - Phase 1:
1. Player Management:
    - Each player has: playerID, username, level (1-100)
    - Track player statistics: total matches played, wins, kills

2. Match Lobby:
    - Support different game modes: SOLO, DUO, SQUAD
    - Lobby capacity:
        SOLO: 100 players
        DUO: 50 teams (100 players)
        SQUAD: 25 teams (100 players)
    - Players can join/leave lobby before match starts

3. Match States:
    - WAITING (lobby is open, players joining)
    - STARTING (countdown begun, no new players)
    - IN_PROGRESS (match ongoing)
    - FINISHED (match completed)

4. Basic Operations:
    - Create a new match lobby
    - Add player to lobby
    - Remove player from lobby
    - Start match (when minimum players reached)
    - End match and declare winner(s)

5. Validation Rules:
    - Minimum players to start:
    - SOLO: 50 players
    - DUO: 20 teams (40 players)
    - SQUAD: 10 teams (40 players)
    - Player cannot join multiple active matches
    - Cannot add players after match starts
    - Squad size must be exactly 4 players, Duo exactly 2





Sample Scenarios:
Create SQUAD match, 10 teams join, match starts
Player tries to join when already in another match
Try to start match with only 5 teams (should fail)
Player leaves lobby before match starts